From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Give a PS4 title's Windows side no standard handles.

Descriptors 0-2 of a PS4 title are not standard streams: nothing reads them,
so whatever a game wrote there was lost. Worse, once one stops taking data a
write to it never ends: it goes async, and the in-process server, which holds
no copy of the descriptor on this console, never sees it become writable.
Bloodlines hung on every Quit that way (2026-11-08, found with the wait
watchdog through 1074): its main thread sat in WriteFile on its stderr handle
with the engine's shutdown warnings.

On __PROSPERO__ get_initial_console now leaves hStdInput, hStdOutput and
hStdError NULL, so writes to them fail at once (C runtimes treat that as no
console), and logs once what descriptors 0-2 are (PW_STD_HANDLES).
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
@@ -1356,6 +1356,34 @@ static void get_initial_console( RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *params )
 {
     int output_fd = -1;
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ A TITLE'S DESCRIPTORS 0-2 ARE NOT STANDARD STREAMS. Nothing on the
+     * console reads them, so what a game writes there was lost anyway, and
+     * once one stops taking data the write never ends: it goes async, and the
+     * server, which holds no copy of the descriptor on this console (it cannot
+     * duplicate one), never sees it become writable. Vampire: The Masquerade
+     * - Bloodlines hung on every Quit that way (2026-11-08): its main thread
+     * sat in WriteFile on its stderr handle with the engine's shutdown
+     * warnings ("Reference Count for Material ... != 0").
+     *
+     * So give Windows no standard handles at all: writing to them fails at
+     * once, which C runtimes treat as no console. Say once what 0-2 are. */
+    {
+        struct stat st;
+        int fd;
+
+        for (fd = 0; fd <= 2; fd++)
+        {
+            if (fstat( fd, &st ))
+                ERR( "PW_STD_HANDLES fd=%d is not open (errno %d)\n", fd, errno );
+            else
+                ERR( "PW_STD_HANDLES fd=%d mode=%o tty=%d: not given to Windows\n",
+                     fd, (unsigned int)st.st_mode, isatty( fd ) );
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
+
     wine_server_fd_to_handle( 0, GENERIC_READ|SYNCHRONIZE,  OBJ_INHERIT, &params->hStdInput );
     wine_server_fd_to_handle( 1, GENERIC_WRITE|SYNCHRONIZE, OBJ_INHERIT, &params->hStdOutput );
     wine_server_fd_to_handle( 2, GENERIC_WRITE|SYNCHRONIZE, OBJ_INHERIT, &params->hStdError );
-- 
